WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.280
Привет!

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:02.000
Датмин Схелоин-Рашен.

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:04.900
Валком-то привет, русский, эписот-секти-тю-ту.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.240
Это в Дюллае, 2026.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.320
Айм Олия, тодей из Лесенн, будет убивать Фануан.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:11.080
О, ехали.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:13.720
Тодей из ворт of the day из Дерева.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:14.420
Дерева.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.780
It sounds like death-ray-e-wo.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.880
Пикчер отол Дерева 3, вэйвинец-бранчив-слаков-ренды-джиант

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:21.540
in the forest.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:23.020
Это большой Дерева.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.280
This is the big tree, repeat after me.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:25.940
Дерева.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.820
Now let's build more words to talk about nature.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.680
Our first new word is река.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:32.080
Река.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.200
It sounds like wreck-ках.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.040
The river is long, река длинная.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.680
Remember, летает from a few lessons ago.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:40.820
It means flies.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:42.600
Next comes Les.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:43.320
Les.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:44.680
It sounds like Les.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:46.740
There are many trees in the forest.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.280
In the forest there are many trees.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.080
Les sounds like leaves.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.760
Perfect for a leafy forest.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:53.300
Let's add гора.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.500
It sounds like gach-rah.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:58.180
The mountain is high, гора высокая.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:00:59.860
Imagine a gach-rah mountain.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.020
So tall it touches the gray muskye.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:03.600
Now we meet цветок.

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:04.400
Цветок.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.080
It sounds like твое ток.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:07.260
The flower is beautiful.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:08.500
Цветок красивый.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:10.980
Цвое ток starts with the sound of color.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:12.660
Because flowers bring color.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.360
Next is птица.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:15.020
Птица.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.780
It sounds like птица цах.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:18.060
The bird is flying.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:19.120
Птица летает.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.400
Remember, летает means flies.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:22.780
Let's meet Рыба.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:23.460
Рыба.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:25.260
It sounds like Ho-ба.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:27.240
The fish swims in the river.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.720
Рыба плавает в реке.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.180
Рыба враем свет рыба.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:32.140
На вылукаб от неба.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:32.820
Неба.

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.600
It sounds like Небо.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:35.760
До скайз блю.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:36.700
Небо сини.

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:37.860
Небо.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:37.980
Небо.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.380
It sounds like Nibaut.

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:41.360
One more pair of words.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:42.020
Трава.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.560
It sounds like трах вах.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:45.000
Дограс из грин.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.160
Трава зеленая.

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:46.700
Трава.

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:47.640
Филс лэк-травэрс.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:48.640
Дограс у наволк.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:49.140
Озеро.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:50.720
It sounds like U-Zero.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.180
The lake is big.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.220
Озеро большое.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.500
U-Zero sounds like U-Zero.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:56.380
Камень.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:57.780
It sounds like Кахмен.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:01:59.020
The stone is heavy.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:00.180
Камень тяжелый.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:02.040
Кахмен sounds like common.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:04.040
Now for a quick grammar bite.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:07.580
Рашен ажектовый must match the gender of the noun they describe.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:08.840
Большое дерево.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:09.840
Ands in Oye.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.480
Because дерево is neuter.

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:12.900
Длинная река.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:13.960
Ands in Aya.

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.460
Because Rika is feminine.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:17.000
Бусокая гора.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:17.500
Also.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:18.460
Ands in Aya.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:19.820
Unlike English.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:21.340
Where big stays the same.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.320
Рашен makes the adjective agree.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:24.940
So the sentence sounds natural.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:27.340
Рашен have a deep love for nature.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:30.600
They often spend weekends in the less or at an озеро.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:34.500
Many sons and poems celebrate the beauty of the Russian landscape.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:38.000
Especially the white birches on famous paintings and fairy tales.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:43.040
For our practice challenge, kids can draw a less with a Rika and treat sweet key.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:46.420
Then label each in Russian and say the word sound loud.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:51.000
Adults look out your window or take a short walk and describe three things.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.180
Using today's words.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:53.680
Like, at a дерево.

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:54.960
Or, не басинея.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.980
Now hear something really cool about one of the day's words.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.020
Want to know a secret about C-talk?

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:04.860
Did you know that the Russian words C-talk and the English word color are actually cousins?

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.800
They both come from the ancient root, meaning to shine or be bright.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:13.200
This word traveled through Slavic languages and became sweet for color.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.280
Then grew into sweet talk for flower.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:18.180
Because flowers are nature's brightest colors.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:19.500
Be careful, though.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:22.360
The color sounds like it could mean color in English.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:24.980
Yet it means both color and the blooming flower.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:27.780
Next time you see a colorful flower, remember.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:29.620
It is cousins with sweet talk.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:31.780
They both come from that shining root.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:35.700
That connection is your secret shortcut to remembering it forever.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:37.200
You did great today.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:40.640
Say today's words out loud one more time and there yours.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.640
Share the show with a friend who wants to learn Russian.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:44.900
And I'll see you next time.

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:47.840
And if you'd rather watch, then listen.

